      "evidence": "Proof 2.1 says “the two models share the exponential law but differ in the prefactor.” The Remark states the rectangular factor equals one when y=E/U=(2±√3)/4. For those admissible fixed parameters, its prefactor 16y(1-y) equals the smooth model’s prefactor 1, so the unqualified claim that they differ is false. The Statement’s qualified claim that the prefactor can differ remains supported.",
